  <prompt>Owner UAT round 8 (2026-10-06), item 1. Record: `notes/042-uat-round8-2026-10-06.md`.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE frontend developer on the Office add-in (React 19, Fluent UI v9).</role>

  <goal>The Send Email action sits in the toolbar right after Find as a mail icon + "Send", in place of the full-width button in the pane body; Word's Email tab reads "Send" too.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      - Outlook's Send Email (task 036) opens Outlook's native compose window; it is an action, not a tab ("Outlook unchanged", task 096). Today it renders as a full-width secondary button above the tab content (`App.tsx` `sendEmailRow`), shown only when there is a document or related record to link (`resolveSendEmailAffordance`).
      - Word's Email tab (task 096, `canEmailFromPane`) is already in the toolbar, labelled "Email".
    </background>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner item 1">Toolbar, directly after Find; mail icon + "Send"; Word's Email tab label becomes "Send".</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 036 / NFR-10">Gating unchanged: capability-only via `resolveSendEmailAffordance`; absent (not disabled) when there is nothing to link; spinner + disabled while sending; errors still shown in the pane body and announced.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 subtle button matching the tabs' size; fits the 320 px minimum pane width with the Expand and ⋮ buttons.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Toolbar tests: Send renders after Find only when supplied, calls the handler, disabled while sending; Word tab label "Send".</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Outlook, after a save: toolbar reads Save · To Do · Find · Send; the body has no Send Email button; clicking Send opens compose as before.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Outlook, before anything is saved/linked: no Send in the toolbar.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Word: the Email tab is labelled "Send" and still opens the in-pane email form.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Gates: full jest green; lint 0; typecheck 0 production.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Toolbar: optional `onSendEmail` / `isSendingEmail` props; render a subtle button after the tab list.</step>
    <step>Shell passes them through; App supplies them when `canSendEmail`, removes the body button, keeps the error bar + live region.</step>
    <step>Word tab label → "Send"; tests; gates; note; POML status.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>Send Email handler and toolbar exist.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — the existing handler is rendered in the existing toolbar.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Owner UAT round 8 item 1: a full-width button takes body space for an action that belongs with the tabs.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

